<task id="183" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>DocumentEmailWizard uses the shared EmailComposer (SemanticSearchControl PCF and DocumentRelationshipViewer hosts)</title>
    <phase>12 Create-wizard lookups and composer (UAT round 4)</phase>
    <gate>after 182 (shared compose helper)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies shared client code (.ts/.tsx) used by several wizards.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Copies an existing composer mount (DocumentEmailStep.tsx) into one wizard; the PCF React 16 host is the known risk.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Depends on 182's helper; one host is a PCF needing its own build and version bump.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>182</deps>
    <tags>pcf, frontend, react, fluent-ui, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>DocumentEmailWizard still renders the old EmailStep directly (review section 2.2, last row). The record exists when it runs, so it can mount the composer the way the Document Upload wizard does (DocumentEmailStep.tsx), and send through the composer.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in React, Fluent UI v9 and the @spaarke/ui-components wizard framework (CreateRecordWizard, WizardShell).</role>
  <goal>DocumentEmailWizard renders EmailComposer (not EmailStep), sends with the same route and mailbox as today, and works in both hosts: the SemanticSearchControl PCF (React 16/17 platform libs) and the DocumentRelationshipViewer code page.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Review section 2.2 and section 4 item 8. DocumentEmailWizard.tsx:44, 818-824, 486-510; hosts SemanticSearchControl.tsx:1911 and DocumentRelationshipViewer App.tsx:830. The composer already runs in the CommunicationActions PCF. Memory note: PCF (React 16/17) vs code page (React 19) type drift in shared components (per-import cast to React.ComponentType).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DocumentEmailWizard/DocumentEmailWizard.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/DocumentUploadWizard/src/components/DocumentEmailStep.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/pcf/SemanticSearchControl/SemanticSearchControl/SemanticSearchControl.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="182" status="pending">composeOnlyText helper and the composer wiring decisions (owner questions 2-4)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">Owner directive 2026-11-12, applies to every file this task touches: reuse the existing side-pane lookup (`DataverseLookupField` over `INavigationService.openLookup`) and the existing `EmailComposer`; never re-create either. A third rendering of the lookup pattern is a defect (review section 4 item 6).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Every component changed in this task stays in `@spaarke/ui-components` and receives Dataverse access only through injected services (`INavigationService`, `IDataService`, `authenticatedFetch`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Every UI change in this task uses Fluent v9 and semantic tokens only; light and dark both fully themed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests added in this task cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in the acceptance criteria; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task notes. No numeric test target.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The PCF host change follows docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md: version bump in every location the pcf-deploy skill lists; build with npm run build:prod.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">Owner D-219 (2026-11-12, notes/decisions.md): From choice, Cc and Bcc, attachments, templates and AI drafting are ON (wire onListEmailTemplates / onDraftWithAi from the host compose handlers, as DocumentEmailStep.tsx:320-322).</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/pcf.md</file>
