    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Composer mount with an existing record" location="src/solutions/DocumentUploadWizard/src/components/DocumentEmailStep.tsx">Lines ~247-330: inline mount, sendMode, associations = the record, createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read DocumentEmailStep.tsx and DocumentEmailWizard.tsx; list today's send fields.</step>
    <step order="2">Replace EmailStep with EmailComposer mounted as in DocumentEmailStep.</step>
    <step order="3">Build the SemanticSearchControl PCF with build:prod and the DocumentRelationshipViewer page; fix React-version type drift by the documented cast only.</step>
    <step order="4">Add tests; run the dev check in both hosts.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the tests named in the acceptance criteria, the touched folders' suites, `npx tsc --noEmit -p .` and ESLint on touched files in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components; all pass.</step>
    <step order="6">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` AND this POML's status element to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 -Project spaarke-ontology-platform-r1`.</step>
    <step order="7">Record any deviation from this POML, and the dev-check result, in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/task-183-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the composer cannot render under the PCF's React 16/17 platform libraries, STOP and escalate (do not fork the composer).</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Document email from Semantic Search">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a matter form with the Semantic Search control on dev</step>
        <step>Select a document, choose Email</step>
        <step>Pick a recipient with the pane, send</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Composer renders inside the PCF dialog, the email is sent and filed as today; light and dark themed; no console errors.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Document email from Document Relationship Viewer">
      <steps>
        <step>Open the viewer on dev</step>
        <step>Email a document</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Same as above in the code page host.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Run jest, tsc and ESLint in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components (npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; in a fresh worktree build ../Spaarke.SdapClient and ../Spaarke.Auth first)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DocumentEmailWizard/DocumentEmailWizard.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DocumentEmailWizard/__tests__/DocumentEmailWizard.composer.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">DocumentEmailWizard renders EmailComposer and no longer imports ../EmailStep.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The composer shows the From choice, Cc, Bcc, attachments, template picker and AI draft in both hosts.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The send request uses the chosen mailbox and carries associations (the record) and the selected documents as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The SemanticSearchControl PCF builds with build:prod and its version is bumped in every location; the DocumentRelationshipViewer page builds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Both hosts pass the dev check; no console errors.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (closed set, every task): no new lookup component, no new email form, no change to the behaviour of the inline `LookupField.tsx`, and no `Xrm` import added to any component file (the host injects `INavigationService`; ADR-012).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All existing tests in the touched folders pass unchanged unless a criterion above names the change; tsc clean; no new ESLint errors in touched files.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes> Source: projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/create-wizard-lookup-composer-review.md (Fable review 2026-11-12) and UAT round 4 findings F-R4-2 / F-R4-3 (notes/uat-v4-log.md).</notes>
